{"title":"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Welcome to the Birthday Problem Set! In this set, there are multiple choice AND free-response questions. Feel free to look at the solutions if you are stuck:\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/f/c1f0a94ea8742b3593b3b394c54f3ad77a4b1de0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lceil {\\frac{3!+4!+5!+6!}{2+3+4+5+6}} \\right \\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"154\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/89135b84ce4ab65534a21b1009c6c69749fa7467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 42\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 43\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 44\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 45\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"G285 MC10B Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afea61bbc7bbc2d72748d6750aa5252ac6dd978a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x,y) = \\begin{cases}x^y &amp; \\text{ if } x^2&gt;y \\text{ and } |x|&lt;y\\\\f(f(\\sqrt{|x|},y),y) &amp; \\text{ otherwise} \\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"395\" height=\"53\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a positive integer, find the sum of all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3dbf51a7e70803e9b69704477aaa79216d3532.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x,y) \\neq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" /> for some constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e68ffba142207af7baf730920006dc8a428a9692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ -1 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 0 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{3}{8} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"400\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_2\" title=\"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> groups of molecules are gathered in a lab. The scientists in the lab randomly assign the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> molecules into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> groups of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Within these groups, there will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distinguishable labels (Strong acid, weak acid, strong base, weak base, nonelectrolyte), and each molecule will randomly be assigned a label such that teams can be empty, and each label is unique in the group. Find the number of ways that the molecules can be arranged by the scientists. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/3/e832f34e92bc819cb87d817e9f7ecb4f473edbf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5^{60} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{60!\\cdot 5^{60}}{(12!)^4} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{60!\\cdot 5^{30}}{(12!)^4} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{40!\\cdot 5^{60}}{11!(12!)^3} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 60!5^{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"570\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_3\" title=\"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> people are attending a hotel conference, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of which are executives, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of which are speakers. Each person is designated a seat at one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> round tables, each containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> seats. If executives must sit at least one speaker and executive, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> ways the people can be seated. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee24ea6c5f0c27cef8a35ec04fe3c6426f1f996.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lfloor \\sqrt{N} \\right \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"46\" height=\"32\" />. Assume seats, people, and table rotations are distinguishable.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d9191bb8b311032342250c9f65fb9014dfa8e5f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 720 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1440 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2520 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 5760\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 6172$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"475\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_4\" title=\"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is an equilateral triangle. Let points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on the extensions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a108fae648fca8e09047d8b1a190a403edf643f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AED=60^o$\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f275f0a7e591579c00f31616e3c481b97cd7d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" />. If there exists a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> outside of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db041d9c0fda44cf24b4f4ae7f02243ef2ea7f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2f9226cfa73a80a0cb28f6b2f936ea3d6f91943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=PD=28$\" width=\"123\" height=\"13\" />, and there exists a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> outside outside of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99bf9f98bdd453a34a3cc3973346bd291e7c8b73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CBDE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15b4b627ec8129ecade96dedeb8e3b1bd6e2c6e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OE=OA$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />, the area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/c/f5c7b1ac8264c3d7ecec2691a520f304c91497c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2APEO$\" width=\"65\" height=\"13\" /> can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/934d983ce99c8feb680dc630ca4ff840167e9ef8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\sqrt{n}+o\\sqrt{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are squarefree,. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b98e3af81cac9c2a1cccaebf281c01972b35dad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+o+p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad3088d2c7a0a50ba0cecae0f69615cf1c5edea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 152 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 162 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 164 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 214\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 224$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a rectangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a4826138756e48059393331c30916b2b06430cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/ccc55f85ae3c39ddd90ace7764a57bce879351c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Let points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be the center of the circumcircle of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e008485112ecedc2a56ed967df7735c814919f7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MNOP$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f1b4e12f3f42a40aeaac905743951907522bf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MNP$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/3/5739fe73a6ce838508b4a3cd7863c26d28008710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MNO$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> respectively, along with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52cd0d6bb3caafbbddb96f479355212f03c8de81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD \\perp QO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/5856c99c2637c3fd6c5dd41049850f8cfbd99360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MP \\perp BP$\" width=\"87\" height=\"12\" />. If the shortest distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/f/e1fcf07989db9ac3eeb06eeab0f34dda033f679c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AOQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/5524ce1987b135eb4a1c84f354c92437452d4941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle QBP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> are degenerate, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b3d69b4bb9fdb7f5feff12af48ec718da4b9ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP=AO$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/9/f7902d584306a361408d3f5265b5cbc56afcf4fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 \\cdot OD \\cdot PC$\" width=\"102\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a50bef490bc251784c9e2576ac90ce57b116cab8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 209 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 228 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 54\\sqrt{57} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 90\\sqrt{19} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 72\\sqrt{57}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"515\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Geometry285 is playing the game \"Guess And Choose\". In this game, Geometry285 selects a subset of not necessarily distinct integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a903cc8aee65f732231e28d6b5894641cd93c18e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=\\{a,b,c \\cdots \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" /> from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d46e81186a8db30d6954aa3022ada2ddbd9934f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\{1,2,3,4 \\cdots k-1,k \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"201\" height=\"18\" /> such that the sum of all elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Each distinct is selected chronologically and placed in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa930fb6109d1a758e438f00ab653466f9428420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le a \\le k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/050f3b67aa525e6464f3d9a28d9b8c760caf6415.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le b \\le a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a98a665e96e0dbe995ef152001ad4da4ff151a0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le c \\le b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" />, and so on. Then, the elements are randomly arranged. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/494677ee3ecbf4872849c42319488cd07fabd578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{p,k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"17\" /> represents the total number of outcomes that a subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> integers sums to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. If distinct permutations of the same set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are considered unique, find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81d362db7cdc458f8ef2ff6b072eda8f82550801.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{p=1}^{1000}\\sum_{k=1}^{1000} S_{p,k}\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"52\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcd47d1e3fe35977c9517c814a0220f11caab732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 50 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 51 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 124$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"385\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a80c0dd28f6214099a65992dc2f666e7b32683a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=x^{12}-9x^{11}+16x^{10}+256x^5+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"301\" height=\"19\" />, Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/a/6bab02e5bc374ab8dd5342129a32618bcb344189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, r_2, r_3, r_4, r_5, r_6, ..., r_{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"186\" height=\"11\" /> be the twelve roots that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/43407f6a2b5d524f6e57c70c914ef7dca7d505b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, find the least possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c48a677ee0d00371d1b64cd7108c8f2dcdea89e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left \\lfloor \\sum_{n=1}^{12}\\sum_{k=1}^{12} r_nr_k-\\sum_{s=1}^{11} r_s \\right \\rfloor\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c5b630c5c21ec55cde5323dcc6656722aac342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 67 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 69 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 70 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 71 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_8\" title=\"G285 Summer Problem Set Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> with centers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> concur at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab50d811662c994a560b367cccc3df420fa136a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/3/0a3de23f6c6984c29b90b181ce2698bbf5c667e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AL=28$\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" />. Suppose a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on the extension of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is formed such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/b/00bae8607efde51a1c5d5217c9a2cc9170355eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ=29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> and lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/9007ebc36bd9988037c41a5aac856635701f5680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PL$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3dfd17b252c7e56a6b467d7d638194dd959b9496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=\\frac{16\\sqrt{37}}{\\sqrt{145}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"108\" height=\"45\" />, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/10548fb0dc4df50846e8dfb5242846207088598d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2(\\angle LAQ)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"22\" /> can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/b/9abc3e34096fb17443e2b5fd50699fecf2e1d5ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m \\sqrt{n}}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"39\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is square free. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/b/0bb496864e104adac8197787c1b2dc0c546c114a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2m+3n+4r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/0/3607b62a93a20f6c9937681d47f82c25cc8bd773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 28 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 31 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 39 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 45 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767a53f43be056f9333f71e3e39f59aa0f8bca35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08ff8ea020546fb6e8c90abbfb0b50802eee802d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/6/0f63b9f05ed23082323ad514618b520a0dcdb015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\omega_k \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/6/c269d02f52692dbe2474ba400d9d9436dfd50f03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=(p_1p_2p_3 \\cdots p_e)^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"19\" /> for distinct prime factors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/7/6072c4c51eae6fd2fe921aed70b9ee71b6374f33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8569597fbeeb665b4eed107b72b03ff2a00c6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/f/67f3a70b1424ac8eff21831ddd3405258bc83dc7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=1}^{e} p_j\\]\" width=\"42\" height=\"49\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0a9cc9827a453a7403b1e5b13bf66527bdbf95b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> must satisfy that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271aa1aba81d335bdd5f1849cfd3ace3e86f606e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\lfloor \\omega_k \\rfloor}{p_j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"38\" height=\"43\" /> is an integer, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0a9cc9827a453a7403b1e5b13bf66527bdbf95b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> is divisible by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />th and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d76bd4a232f2d7216a6cd53196e566f1e086eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />th triangular number. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc28eba9e2b0a59bdc44b0fcc106c8f79af23d60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(3)+\\tau(4)+\\tau(5)+ \\cdots +\\tau(99)+\\tau(100)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"324\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793df57b3f72cda8eaba4615c74c4dee9baf900e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1024 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1331 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 1539 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2000 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2719$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"484\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let a recursive sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> be defined such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fdf8f14967b492a8b1ee72bca8c9e34c37e55ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e256f9f50dc62ade5023adc7cb1ebd5ed75d5daf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=16a_{n-1}+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"15\" />. Find the last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dcd9ab7664268badb6f02aced18add052b02f5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"28\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC-IME_I_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 2021 MC-IME I Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/97078445d982c94143f1158f5f693e4ca3c6110a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(a,b,c)=a^2b^4+b^2c^4+c^2a^4+8c+8b+8a+8a^3+8b^3+8c^3-3\\sqrt[3]{abc}-21\\]\" width=\"524\" height=\"22\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e666a62eaf9f4bc63d561d6b572002fe859bdf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a)+P(b)+P(c)=P(a,b,c)=P(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"310\" height=\"18\" />, and the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a2f7534d08cd1d4672bef4ce465aa829667750f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> contains the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13ac160364162e5c6c0737a8e0361bf1a774c528.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(P(k),P(k)+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/e/71ed7ec75b3b530feafeceb88fe334d50880662a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(P(k)+3,P(k)+5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d82da86b1cb2fc0273954fee60ec20969c299706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(P(k)+8,11)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />, find the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d5f8b3af68cef2cad3ceca80b211fd81cc79551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(23)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e3859e3c705b4c621f0161e2c3dafdeb7ccd44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(P(P(a,b,c))=abc(P(a)+P(b)+P(c))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b6f63aa2266ef1b39b31386bd17b28e25faaac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> concur at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/6/f06175de06075b060abdf04ebd2ecfe88e58fc97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EP$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is the common chord shared by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c2ebe718e80cbb69571246e73cdcbfe9522810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{O_1,O_3 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/9/089ed8a955d97f704030f6a1e9350a3f3a466437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> is the common chord shared by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351e049c4623c6f7d8ff708e872c29400b737f84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{O_1,O_2 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the common internal tangent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50cb6417d8a7ba0a14f80a6667f918fad51c916f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{O_2,O_3 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />. Let the extension of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0edebe902653b343eee6f0a6a93a09f80884504e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/9/089ed8a955d97f704030f6a1e9350a3f3a466437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b6f63aa2266ef1b39b31386bd17b28e25faaac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb9fee7cc7b4044db1570d99ce54a05428cd723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CF} \\cap \\overline{BG} \\in D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" />, prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/4/e7425d4a658260a4de266630c22fbbed6c55aa57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABDC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is a parallelogram.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Bobby the frog is hopping around the unit circle. Suppose Bobby starts at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a306093bbd9e0699c65dba033c9483cd379dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. After every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th minute, Bobby moves to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff7653c925c7a4b51f04d92a9741b83a0c55cc25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,bi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c0a13ee3ff90dd3f56407221c06ab07e141be3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2 \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff7653c925c7a4b51f04d92a9741b83a0c55cc25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,bi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> is an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th root of unity for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />. Suppose Bobby is unidirectional for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes, and randomly chooses to reverse his direction after each cycle. In how many ways can Bobby travel around the unit circle exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the average of all values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c0e1a56d22832227717e1018fa00be730d2adf0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{n=1}^{119} \\prod_{j=1}^{7} (z^j)^{n} = \\left(\\sum_{p=1}^{60} z^{2p-1}-\\sum_{n=1}^{59} z^{2n} \\right)^{5040}+2\\]\" width=\"346\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_Summer_Problem_Set_Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 2021 Summer Problem Set Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017101831\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.058 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.076 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 905/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 31159/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21513:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017101831 and revision id 157031. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}